# SABOTAGE: MG-13 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Vault.Change.resolve_subject_id/1`'s
# fall-back to the row's EXISTING primary key is severed (`changeset.data || %{}` → `&&`,
# which yields the empty map for any real changeset). The lookup then always misses and the
# function GENERATES A FRESH UUID, so re-vaulting a field on an UPDATE files the new
# ciphertext under a subject that belongs to NO ROW.
#
# That is a silent crypto-shred hole, not a crash: the write succeeds, the column gets a
# valid token, reveal still works (reveal keys on the token). What is lost is the invariant
# the subject exists for — `Samen.Erasure.shred/2` deletes by SUBJECT, so a shred of the
# row's own id leaves that ciphertext decryptable behind it. Nothing about the domain row
# looks wrong; only the `pii_vault.subject_id` of the re-vaulted value does.
#
# Flips the named MG-13 red, which asserts the vault row's subject equals the record's pk
# both on the initial create and after the update. The create arm is UNAFFECTED by this
# patch (on create the lookup misses either way and a fresh subject is correct), which is
# what makes the update assertion the discriminating one.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the identical `||` in `ensure_subject_attr/2` (a different
# clause, one line later in that function's cond), the pk-change arm above, and `pk_attr/1`.
#
# One boolean operator. Touches vault/change.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/vault_change_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-13: re-vaulting a field on an UPDATE files the ciphertext under the row's own pk
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Vault.Change do
         to_string(value)
 
       _ ->
-        case Map.get(changeset.data || %{}, pk) do
+        case Map.get(changeset.data && %{}, pk) do
           nil -> Ash.UUID.generate()
           existing -> to_string(existing)
         end
